{% comment %}
  Color Role Resolver
  ------------------------------------------------------------------------------

  Purpose:
  The single owner of colour-ROLE resolution, the sibling of
  `snippets/typography-resolver.liquid` (which owns role-based type but never
  emits `color`). Like `accent-resolver`, it outputs BARE CSS declarations --
  no selector, no braces -- so it drops straight into a `{% style %}` rule or a
  `style=""` attribute.

  ------------------------------------------------------------------------------

  THE CONTRACT IT IMPLEMENTS

  Custom properties inherit. The scheme roles (`--color-heading`,
  `--color-text`, `--color-soft-text`, `--color-link`, `--color-border` and the
  accent trio) are declared once on the section's `.color-<scheme>` element, and
  every block below reads them at paint time. A child theme block cannot read a
  parent's settings in Liquid -- but it does not need to: a CARD redeclares
  those same role names on its own surface, and every nested block follows with
  no per-block change.

  That is the whole mechanism. This snippet owns both ends of it:

    context mode  a card sets the colour context for its subtree
    color mode    a leaf reads the role token that context may have repointed

  ------------------------------------------------------------------------------

  MODE: 'context'  -- called by a card on its own surface rule

  Required:
    source {Object}  Caller settings, carrying `content_color` plus, on
                     'accent', the shared ids `accent_selected`
                     (neutral|soft|strong) and `accent_contrast`
                     (subtle|filled).

  Optional (override the matching `source` values, for a card whose own
  settings use other ids or fix the accent, e.g. a "Card colour" of Accent
  that always means the neutral accent, filled):
    content_color   {String}  scheme | accent | custom
    accent          {String}  neutral | soft | strong
    accent_contrast {String}  subtle | filled

    {% render 'color-role-resolver', mode: 'context', source: block.settings,
       content_color: 'accent', accent: 'neutral', accent_contrast: 'filled' %}

  `content_color` values:

    scheme (default)
      Emits NOTHING. The section scheme's roles stand untouched, so roles stay
      distinct (heading / text / soft text are three different colours) and a
      card nested inside an already-accented parent keeps inheriting it. This
      must stay a true no-op -- re-asserting the same values would break that,
      and it CANNOT be a reset: once a role is shadowed the scheme's original
      value is unrecoverable from a descendant.

      That is safe only because no card accepts another card as a child (their
      accept-lists are leaf blocks plus the background-less _group), so an
      opaque scheme-coloured surface can never sit inside an accented one and
      inherit a foreground that does not suit its own ground. If a card ever
      gains a card child, this branch needs scheme-value aliases emitted in
      layout/theme.liquid to reset against.

    accent
      Resolves the chosen accent into the CARD-LOCAL `--surface-accent` family,
      then repoints the shared roles for the subtree. The card paints its own
      background from `--surface-accent*`, which is what makes the `filled`
      inversion safe: repointing `--color-accent` for the children cannot feed
      back into the card's own fill.

      Hierarchy is carried by ALPHA, not by hue. On an accent ground there is
      only one foreground guaranteed to be legible, so soft text is a fade of
      that foreground rather than a different colour.

      On `filled` the accent trio is INVERTED for the subtree. A nested Button
      paints `background: var(--color-accent)`; on an accent-filled card that is
      accent-on-accent and disappears. Inverted, it comes back as
      contrast-on-accent. `subtle` needs no swap -- accent on the contrast
      ground already reads.

    custom
      The card's own four pickers.

  The snippet never sets `background-color`: background ownership stays with the
  block, matching `snippets/background-role-token.liquid`. The caller reads
  `var(--surface-accent)` (filled) or `var(--surface-accent-contrast)` (subtle)
  for its ground.

  Usage:
    .card--{{ block.id }} {
      {% render 'color-role-resolver', mode: 'context', source: block.settings %}
      background-color: {{ surface_bg }};
      border: 1px solid var(--color-border);
    }

  ------------------------------------------------------------------------------

  MODE: 'color'  -- called by a leaf block

  Required:
    role   {String}  'heading' | 'text' | 'soft' | 'accent'. The role the block
                     plays, used to resolve `auto`.
    source {Object}  Caller settings, carrying `text_color`.

  Emits exactly one `color:` declaration.

    auto (default)  var(--color-<role>) -- the token a card may have repointed
    heading         var(--color-heading)
    text            var(--color-text)
    soft            var(--color-soft-text)
    accent          var(--color-accent)
    parent          inherit (the CSS keyword)

  Usage:
    #heading-{{ id }} {
      {% render 'typography-resolver', role: 'heading', source: source %}
      {% render 'color-role-resolver', mode: 'color', role: 'heading', source: source %}
    }

  ------------------------------------------------------------------------------

  SCHEMA CONTRACT

  Card (context mode). `visible_if` does not parse parentheses -- keep the
  chains flat.

    { "type": "header", "content": "Content Color" },
    {
      "type": "select",
      "id": "content_color",
      "label": "Content Color",
      "info": "Accent paints the card in the selected accent and recolors every block inside it.",
      "options": [
        { "value": "scheme", "label": "Color Scheme" },
        { "value": "accent", "label": "Accent" },
        { "value": "custom", "label": "Custom" }
      ],
      "default": "scheme"
    },
    {
      "type": "select",
      "id": "accent_selected",
      "label": "Accent",
      "options": [
        { "value": "neutral", "label": "Neutral" },
        { "value": "soft", "label": "Soft" },
        { "value": "strong", "label": "Strong" }
      ],
      "default": "neutral",
      "visible_if": "{{ block.settings.content_color == 'accent' }}"
    },
    {
      "type": "select",
      "id": "accent_contrast",
      "label": "Accent Contrast",
      "info": "Filled paints the accent as the card background. Subtle inverts it.",
      "options": [
        { "value": "subtle", "label": "Subtle" },
        { "value": "filled", "label": "Filled" }
      ],
      "default": "filled",
      "visible_if": "{{ block.settings.content_color == 'accent' }}"
    }

  Leaf (color mode):

    {
      "type": "select",
      "id": "text_color",
      "label": "Color",
      "info": "Automatic follows this block's own role, so a card set to Accent recolors it.",
      "options": [
        { "value": "auto", "label": "Automatic" },
        { "value": "heading", "label": "Heading" },
        { "value": "text", "label": "Text" },
        { "value": "soft", "label": "Soft Text" },
        { "value": "accent", "label": "Accent" },
        { "value": "parent", "label": "Inherit From Parent" }
      ],
      "default": "auto"
    }

{% endcomment %}

{%- liquid
  assign crr_mode = mode | default: 'context'
  assign crr_content = content_color | default: source.content_color
  assign crr_treatment = accent_contrast | default: source.accent_contrast
-%}

{%- if crr_mode == 'color' -%}
  {%- liquid
    assign crr_role = role | default: 'text'
    assign crr_choice = source.text_color | default: 'auto'

    if crr_choice == 'auto'
      assign crr_choice = crr_role
    endif

    case crr_choice
      when 'heading'
        assign crr_color = 'var(--color-heading)'
      when 'soft'
        assign crr_color = 'var(--color-soft-text)'
      when 'accent'
        assign crr_color = 'var(--color-accent)'
      when 'parent'
        assign crr_color = 'inherit'
      else
        assign crr_color = 'var(--color-text)'
    endcase
  -%}
color: {{ crr_color }};

{%- elsif crr_content == 'accent' -%}
  {%- liquid
    # Foreground and ground swap with the treatment. The border follows the
    # foreground on a filled card (a scheme border would vanish into the fill)
    # and the accent's own border role on a subtle one.
    if crr_treatment == 'subtle'
      assign crr_fg = 'var(--surface-accent)'
      assign crr_border = 'var(--surface-accent-border)'
      assign crr_accent = 'var(--surface-accent)'
      assign crr_accent_contrast = 'var(--surface-accent-contrast)'
      assign crr_accent_border = 'var(--surface-accent-border)'
    else
      assign crr_fg = 'var(--surface-accent-contrast)'
      assign crr_border = 'color-mix(in srgb, var(--surface-accent-contrast) 30%, transparent)'
      assign crr_accent = 'var(--surface-accent-contrast)'
      assign crr_accent_contrast = 'var(--surface-accent)'
      assign crr_accent_border = 'var(--surface-accent-contrast)'
    endif
  -%}
{% render 'accent-resolver', source: source, accent: accent, prefix: 'surface-accent' %}
--color-heading: {{ crr_fg }};
--color-text: {{ crr_fg }};
--color-link: {{ crr_fg }};
--color-soft-text: color-mix(in srgb, {{ crr_fg }} 70%, transparent);
--color-border: {{ crr_border }};
--color-accent: {{ crr_accent }};
--color-accent-contrast: {{ crr_accent_contrast }};
--color-accent-border: {{ crr_accent_border }};

{%- elsif crr_content == 'custom' -%}
--color-heading: {{ source.custom_heading_color }};
--color-text: {{ source.custom_text_color }};
--color-link: {{ source.custom_accent_color }};
--color-soft-text: color-mix(in srgb, {{ source.custom_text_color }} 70%, transparent);
--color-border: {{ source.custom_border_color }};
--color-accent: {{ source.custom_accent_color }};
--color-accent-contrast: {{ source.custom_background_color }};
--color-accent-border: {{ source.custom_accent_color }};
{%- endif -%}
